+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held a strong
+close rate of 93.7% on 1,250 opened tickets, and security resolved 95.0% of
+detected incidents. The Q3 delivery plan, kicked off October 5, is on track
+to launch October 23, accounting for weekends and the company planning-day
+holiday on October 12.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+Two figures in the source packets do not match their underlying data and
+should be corrected in the source dashboards:
+
+- **Finance:** the packet's stated total spend of $463,250 does not match
+  the sum of its own line items (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 +
+  Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650 = $464,000). The figures above use
+  the correct summed total, which also shifts the operating surplus to
+  $256,000.
+- **Support:** the packet's stated close rate of 96.4% does not match
+  1,171 closed / 1,250 opened, which computes to 93.7%. The figure above
+  uses the correct computed rate.
+- **Delivery:** the packet's stated launch date of 2026-10-22 undercounts
+  the Release phase. Walking the plan day-by-day from the October 5 start
+  (3 business days Discovery, 6 Build, 4 QA, 1 Release, skipping weekends
+  and the October 12 holiday) puts QA's end on October 22 and Release
+  landing the next business day, October 23. The figure above uses the
+  corrected launch date.
+
+Security's reported 95.0% resolution rate (76 of 80 incidents) checks out
+and needs no correction.
